    "",
    "# Part 3. Authority: what the agent may do in the Company's name",
    "",
    "## 5. The rules every grant obeys",
    "",
    "5.1 The agent has only the authority Schedule A grants it. Neither the existence of the Legal Body, nor anything Novi Corpus publishes about it, nor the Agent Identity itself, is evidence of any other authority. An act of the agent outside a grant is not the Company's act under this Charter unless the Guardian Wallet also signs it.",
    "",
    "5.2 A grant is positive, bounded and specific. It states, for each of the following kinds of act, whether the agent may do it: entering agreements for services the Company provides; accepting an engagement; issuing an invoice in the Company's name; receiving payment to the wallet named in Schedule B; buying goods or services; paying; engaging a contractor for work. For each kind it allows, other than receiving payment, it names the amount up to which the agent may act alone, per act and, for buying, paying and engaging a contractor, per thirty days; and whether, above that amount, the act is allowed with the Guardian Wallet's signature beside the agent's or is not allowed. An invoice is payable only to the wallet named in Schedule B. The amount of an act is the whole value the Company commits to or receives by it; an act whose whole value cannot be stated when it is made is above every amount. Thirty days are counted back from the time of the act. Amounts are stated in USDC, or the same value at the time of the act. A grant names the counterparties it covers and when it starts and ends. What a grant does not name is not granted.",
