    "",
    "5.6 Four kinds of act bind the Company for long: employing a person; borrowing; guaranteeing anyone's obligation; and transferring or encumbering the Company's property, other than paying within a grant. A grant states, for each of them, one of three things: that it is not allowed; that it is allowed only with the Guardian Wallet's signature beside the agent's; or that the agent may do it alone up to an amount the grant names, per act, and above that amount only with the Guardian Wallet's signature beside the agent's. Where a grant says nothing about one of them, it is not allowed. An act is made \"with the Guardian Wallet's signature beside the agent's\" when the Guardian Wallet signs the same document as the Agent Key, in the form published in the record.",
